.TH ZERODDS-XMLC 1 "June 2026" "ZeroDDS 1.0.0-rc.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-xmlc \- DDS-XML validator, deployment renderer, type lister
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-xmlc
.I command
.I file.xml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-xmlc
is a command-line front-end over the ZeroDDS DDS-XML parsers (OMG
DDS-XML 1.0). It parses a deployment file and reports; it never touches
the network.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate \fIFILE.xml\fR
Check well-formedness and parse every DDS-XML library (types, qos,
domain, participant, application). Print a one-line tally. Exit 1 on a
parse or validation error.
.TP
.B render \fIFILE.xml\fR
Print a structured deployment summary: domains and their topics,
participants and their publishers/subscribers with the data
writers/readers underneath.
.TP
.B types \fIFILE.xml\fR
List the
.B <types>
(XTypes) definitions, recursing into modules.
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success / valid.
.TP
.B 1
Parse or validation error.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error / bad invocation.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a deployment file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
zerodds-xmlc validate deployment.xml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Render the deployment tree:
.PP
.RS
.nf
zerodds-xmlc render deployment.xml
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-admin (1),
.BR zerodds-idlc (1)
